From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:36:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix #19578 - Add DELIMITER to the query shown after saving a
 routine, event or trigger

After a procedure, function, event or trigger is created or edited, the
success message shows the executed CREATE statement without a DELIMITER.
When the body contains ";", that query cannot be run again from the SQL
tab, the "Edit" links or the mysql client.

Wrap the displayed CREATE statement in "DELIMITER $$ ... $$ DELIMITER ;",
like the routine and trigger export already does. In edit mode the DROP
statement stays before the DELIMITER line. The query sent to the server
is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
